  "implementation": [
    "Public/private/handoff audio expose explicit complete_step_up and cancellation plus a pending required-assurance accessor. A correlated challenge is reported as step-up-required rather than a malformed protocol result. No credential is issued or inherited.",
    "The original owned reader remains the sole frame/signature verifier. A bounded original-response/scope/assurance expectation exempts exactly one matching signed verified-step-up transition from terminal handling; it confers no authority and cannot extend time by itself.",
    "The foreground validates session owner/profile/token/expiry, scope and previous/current/reason before marking the observed transition verified and renewing the reader deadline under the unchanged original server-key pin. Partial framed reads are not restarted.",
    "Expectation custody clears on every exit. If a transition was observed without complete foreground validation the physical peer retires; late transitions after definitive refusal remain terminal. Presend cancellation retains the original challenge, and its original deadline is not extended."
  ],
  "controlled_signed_quic_assertions": [
    "Successful owned completion preserves the original command scope/envelope/logical identity without resending it; it installs one successor session and remains usable beyond the predecessor reader expiry.",
    "Foreign owner/profile, wrong assurance/token/expiry/scope/previous/reason/correlation, change before session, duplicate session, original reply before authentication, missing frames and streaming beyond the original deadline retire uncertainty.",
    "Definitive refusal retains the original session and consumes the challenge; interrupted execution preserves its distinct original unknown result.",
    "Cancellation after response closes partial transition without installing its candidate; presend cancellation preserves the challenge and original expiry.",
    "A signed late candidate session/change after definitive refusal closes the original peer without extending its deadline or installing its token."
  ],
